# Board game architecture rules

This is a Godot 4 turn-based board game.

The game should be built as a headless rules engine first.

## Core principle

The UI is only a window into the game. The game itself is the state machine.

## Architecture rules

- Build the game as a headless rules engine first.
- The core game must be playable without UI, scenes, buttons, mouse input, sprites, animation, or rendering.
- Keep all core rules under `godot_game/core/` (or `res://core/` within the Godot project).
- Keep visual/debug UI under `godot_game/ui/`.
- Core code should be deterministic from a seed.
- The same seed plus the same legal actions must always produce the same result.
- Rules should mutate `GameState` only through explicit rule functions.
- Rule functions should return events describing what happened.
- The UI must only read state and events; it must not contain rules logic.
- Always add or update tests for any rule change.
- Prefer small, focused files over large monolithic scripts.
- Do not invent extra game systems unless asked.
- Do not build the full game in one pass.

## Game concept

This is a competitive civilisation-building board game on a hex map.

It combines:

- Settlers of Catan-style city-adjacent resource production.
- Pandemic-style heroes moving around the board to contain a spreading demonic underworld.
- Seven Wonders-style drafting of development cards, which are built into cities as special buildings.

## Current project state (2026-06, post Run A merge)

The headless milestone is **complete and extended**. Production branch is `main` @ `a0dda56` (PR #1). Active Godot project: `godot_game/`.

**Implemented in core (test-covered):**

- Seeded radius-3 hex board, players, cities, production, roads, heroes
- Demon spread, breach loss, victory-point win
- Legal actions, bots, event log, deterministic simulation
- `BotGameSession`, CSV export, macro training env + telemetry export
- Development catalog stub, headless card combat (legacy smoke)
- Spell catalogue, combatant spell loadouts, `SpellCombatSession`, micro combat telemetry
- Godot verification scripts (`scripts/Invoke-GodotHeadless.ps1`)

**Implemented in presentation (read-only / bot-advance):**

- Headless CSV/batch/telemetry run modes
- 3D wizard-world board visualisation with overlay
- 2D strategic read-only board mode (`strategic_2d_mode.tscn`)
- Legacy debug event-log overlay

**Not yet implemented:**

- Human macro player action selection (M22 deferred)
- Bank trade, 2D audit mode, 3D combat replay/playable micro
- Full drafting and development-card library
- Full embodied wizard/combat gameplay loop
- Neural network training loop (telemetry export only)

See `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `docs/NEXT_MILESTONES.md` for handoff details.

## Do not build yet

Do not build these until specifically requested:

- Drafting (full Seven Wonders-style system)
- Full development-card library beyond the current stub
- Neural network training
- Finished art, animation, and polish
- Multiplayer networking
- A second parallel GameState or donor-project merge